    "title": "Security & Encryption Format v2",
    "description": "Understanding SaaSBase's military-grade HKDF encryption format and secret management at rest.",
    "content": "Security is the cornerstone of SaaSBase. All sensitive information—including SSH private keys, database passwords, environment variables, API tokens, and backup destination credentials—is encrypted at rest.\n\n## Encryption v2 Specification\n\nSaaSBase uses **Versioned Encryption (Format v2)**:\n* **Algorithm:** AES-256-CBC.\n* **Key Derivation:** HKDF (HMAC-based Extract-and-Expand Key Derivation Function) with SHA-256.\n* **Payload Structure:** `v2:<salt>:<iv>:<ciphertext>`.\n\n```typescript\n// Concept of SaaSBase v2 Encryption\nconst derivedKey = hkdf(masterEncryptionKey, salt, \"saasbase-v2-encryption\");\nconst cipher = crypto.createCipheriv(\"aes-256-cbc\", derivedKey, iv);\n```\n\n## Key Rotation\nIf your master encryption key is ever compromised, SaaSBase provides an atomic key rotation script:\n\n```bash\ndocker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml run --rm \\\n  -e OLD_ENCRYPTION_KEY='old-32-byte-hex-key' \\\n  -e ENCRYPTION_KEY='new-32-byte-hex-key' \\\n  app bun scripts/rotate-encryption-key.ts\n```",
