    "title": "Server Connections (SSH & Host Mode)",
    "description": "How SaaSBase manages remote VPS machines via SSH and the local host machine using nsenter.",
    "content": "SaaSBase manages two distinct types of server environments:\n\n## 1. Remote Servers (SSH2)\nRemote servers are connected over SSH using public-key cryptography (Ed25519 or RSA).\n* Keys are generated inside SaaSBase or imported by the user.\n* Private keys and passphrases are encrypted at rest using AES-256-CBC.\n* SaaSBase executes commands, monitors container metrics, and transfers files through SFTP sessions.\n\n## 2. Localhost Server (Host Mode)\nThe server where SaaSBase itself is running can be bootstrapped as a managed target node (*Localhost*).\n* SaaSBase runs inside a Docker container with `privileged: true` and `pid: host`.\n* It utilizes `nsenter` to execute maintenance commands and interact with the host system and Docker socket directly without needing an SSH loopback connection.",
    "_meta": {
      "filePath": "en\\core-concepts\\server-connections.md",
      "fileName": "server-connections.md",
      "directory": "en\\core-concepts",
      "extension": "md",
      "path": "en\\core-concepts\\server-connections"
    },
    "slug": "core-concepts/server-connections",
    "locale": "en",
    "section": "core-concepts",
    "html": "<p>SaaSBase manages two distinct types of server environments:</p>\n<h2>1. Remote Servers (SSH2)</h2>\n<p>Remote servers are connected over SSH using public-key cryptography (Ed25519 or RSA).</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Keys are generated inside SaaSBase or imported by the user.</li>\n<li>Private keys and passphrases are encrypted at rest using AES-256-CBC.</li>\n<li>SaaSBase executes commands, monitors container metrics, and transfers files through SFTP sessions.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2. Localhost Server (Host Mode)</h2>\n<p>The server where SaaSBase itself is running can be bootstrapped as a managed target node (<em>Localhost</em>).</p>\n<ul>\n<li>SaaSBase runs inside a Docker container with <code>privileged: true</code> and <code>pid: host</code>.</li>\n<li>It utilizes <code>nsenter</code> to execute maintenance commands and interact with the host system and Docker socket directly without needing an SSH loopback connection.</li>\n</ul>"
